     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (some references say 2,000 to 3,000 mg/day). A single 1,700 mg dose also exceeds the usual maximum per dose of about 850 to 1,000 mg. At this dose the risks include severe GI intolerance and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **500 mg** three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily\n- **Something else**\n\nIf you confirm the dose you intended, I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, tell me and I'll add a note documenting that you confirmed it. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
